# Domain and Data Safety

This product includes firms/tenants, users and roles, jewelry products, variants, precious metals, purity/milyem definitions, price calculations, supplier offers and price contracts.

Rules:
- Do not invent business rules from labels or assumptions.
- Verify statuses and choices from backend code/API contract.
- Never treat frontend visibility as authorization.
- Never bypass backend tenant isolation.
- Do not expose internal audit/ownership fields to customer-facing screens unless explicitly approved.
- The inspected product model describes `olusturan_firma` as an audit field that must not be shown to buyers; respect this constraint in buyer-facing UI.
- Price calculation authority remains backend unless a documented contract explicitly says otherwise.
- Do not silently overwrite immutable/versioned price contracts. The inspected contract model documents version creation for changed terms; reflect the verified workflow.
- Preserve numeric precision and rounding rules from backend.
- Treat tax, supplier, buyer, pricing and approval data as sensitive business information.
- Avoid logging secrets or personal/business data unnecessarily.
